language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Graceful labelling of a graph with n nodes and m edges: node labels are distinct values from 0 to m, and the edge labels |f(x) - f(y)| are all different, so they are the values 1 to m.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(1..)
given graph : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..2)] of int(0..n-1)
find nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..m)
find edges : matrix indexed by [int(1..m)] of int(1..m)

branching on [nodes]

such that
$ each node gets a different label
allDiff(nodes),
$ each edge label is the difference between the labels of the two nodes it joins
forAll e : int(1..m) . ((edges[e] = nodes[graph[e,1]+1] - nodes[graph[e,2]+1]) \/ (edges[e] = nodes[graph[e,2]+1] - nodes[graph[e,1]+1])),
$ the edge labels are all different
allDiff(edges)
